   "daf": "30b",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "סוֹמְכוֹס אוֹמֵר בְּחוּלִּין. וְאִילּוּ לַנָּזִיר בְּיַיִן לָא פְּלִיג, מַאי טַעְמָא — אֶפְשָׁר דְּמִתְּשִׁיל אַנְּזִירוּתֵיהּ.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «Summakhos» disagrees and «says:» One may not establish an eiruv for an Israelite with teruma, but only «with» regular, «non-sacred» food items. The Gemara notes: «But» with regard to the mishna’s ruling that an eiruv may be established for «a nazirite with wine,» Summakhos «does not» appear to «disagree. What is the reason» for the distinction? The Gemara explains: A nazirite «can ask» a Sage to annul his vow and release him from «his nazirite status,» and then he himself will be able to drink the wine."
  }
